    "eventMetadata": {
      "context_description": "Hong Kong Observatory's latest 9-day forecast, updated May 4, directly drives trader consensus toward a 24\u00b0C high on May 5 at 42% implied probability, with 25\u00b0C close behind at 31.5%, reflecting mainly cloudy skies, occasional showers, and isolated thunderstorms under a persistent northeast monsoon bringing cooler air from Guangdong. Upper-air disturbances are suppressing solar heating via extensive cloud cover and precipitation, capping daytime temperatures below seasonal May norms of around 29\u00b0C, though easing showers later could nudge peaks slightly higher. Winds from the east at force 4-5 offshore further moderate warmth. Traders anticipate HKO's 11:30 HKT update and multi-model runs for refinements, as the monsoon moderates midweek.",
